# Huatli, Poet of Unity // Roar of the Fifth People, the whole cycle. Turn 1: Huatli ({2}{G}, three Moxen) enters and her trigger
# fetches the Forest (revealed, the library shuffled); the Grizzly Bears is not a basic land card. Turn 3: {3}{R/W}{R/W} is paid exactly with Black Lotus (RRR),
# Mox Jet and Mox Sapphire; she is exiled and returns as the Saga (CR 712.14a) with one lore counter, her front ETB not firing again
# (the hand gains no second land), and chapter I makes two 3/3 green Dinosaur tokens. Turn 5, chapter II: every creature Bot1 controls
# - a token, the Ornithopter - taps for R, G or W (never U), the Saga itself, not a creature, has no mana ability, and Bot2's
# Thrashing Brontodon (cast turn 6, usable turn 8) has none. Turn 7, chapter III: the Dinosaur search finds Thrashing Brontodon, not
# the Grizzly Bears or an Island, the tokens' mana helps cast it. Turn 9, chapter IV: Bot1's Dinosaurs - tokens and Brontodon - gain double strike
# and trample until end of turn; Ornithopter and Bot2's Brontodon do not; the Saga is then sacrificed and the mana ability goes, and a second Brontodon cast after IV resolved gets nothing (only the Dinosaurs there as it resolved).

